</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>LMT = Linear Motor Transport. Positive control means the product is mechanically held or pushed at a fixed pitch rather than spaced by belt friction. See the <a href="/resources/conveyor-cost-guide/">cost guide</a> for cost factors.</p>
<SpecChecklist id="spec-checklist" title="Infeed transition specification checklist" items={[
  ["Products", "Dimensions, weight, shape, material, and stability (tall or tippy, empty or filled) for every SKU."],
  ["Machine interface", "Machine make and model, pitch, pocket or lug spacing, infeed height, and handoff point."],
  ["Rates", "Machine speed range in products per minute, current and planned peak."],
  ["Incoming flow", "How product arrives: random, back-pressured, single file, or multi-lane, and the line conveyor speed."],
  ["Infeed method", "Timing screw, starwheel, servo belts, flights, or independent carts, and why."],
  ["Changeover", "Number of SKUs, changeovers per shift, target changeover time, and which parts change per SKU."],
  ["Hold-back and buffering", "What happens when the machine stops: gates, accumulation length, and restart behavior."],
  ["Controls and signals", "PLC platform, machine-to-conveyor signals (running, starved, blocked), and state model such as PackML."],
  ["Outfeed", "Discharge speed, product stability after the machine, and downstream accumulation."],
  ["Sanitation and materials", "Washdown or dry, food or drug contact requirements, and contact part materials."],
  ["Safety", "Guarding of nip points, screws, and starwheels, and access for changeover."],
  ["Acceptance test", "Run test with each SKU at rated speed, allowed jam and reject rate, and measured changeover time."]
]} />
